---
# Which of the nine languages this project writes in. Without it the checks
# guess from the stylesheet link, which fails on a page that has not been
# written yet.
skill: anthropic

# true when this project's pages are written in one language.
#
# The bilingual rule (cross-skill-rules.md §G) exists because sky-skills
# publishes a bilingual site. A project writing internal docs in one language
# never agreed to it, and without this line every page under docs/ fails every
# run until someone remembers to type --allow-monolingual. Omit it (or write
# false) and the rule applies as before.
#
# This is not a waiver. A waiver says "we saw this finding and chose to live
# with it"; this says "that rule is not about us", which is a different claim
# and is why it is a separate field.
monolingual: false

# Findings this project has looked at and decided to live with.
#
# A waiver DOWNGRADES an error to a warning. It never hides one — the finding
# is still printed, with the reason underneath. Something you chose to accept
# is still something the next person should see.
#
# check   <gate>:<kind>. Ids come from the run itself: visual-audit prints the
#         kind in brackets, axe prints its rule name, interaction prints its
#         own. A check id that does not exist fails validation, so a rename
#         upstream shows up here rather than silently doing nothing.
# reason  Required, and long enough to be one. This is what makes a waiver
#         reviewable instead of a mute button.
# until   Optional YYYY-MM-DD. After that date the waiver fails validation and
#         the decision has to be made again.
waivers:
  - check: visual-audit:figure-no-caption
    reason: the figures here are section headers, so a caption would repeat the h2 above it
    until: 2026-12-31
---

